.TH CTI-FALCON 1 "2026-11-18" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-falcon \- check the fleet's CrowdStrike Falcon API client, and ask Falcon Discover what we run
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti\-falcon \-\-check
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.br
.B cti\-falcon \-\-find\-app
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-vendor
.IR VENDOR ]
.RB [ \-\-exact ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-rows
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B cti\-falcon \-\-new\-apps
.I DAYS
.RB [ \-\-max\-rows
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-falcon
is a read-only check, run by hand. It is the first step of advisory triage
from the organisation's own data. Triage will read three things from Falcon:
the applications we run, which hosts saw an indicator, and which ATT&CK
techniques our detections fired on. Before any of that is built,
.B \-\-check
proves the API client works.
.PP
It gets an OAuth2 token, then makes one
.B limit=1
read per scope on the exact route triage will call:
.TP
.B Hosts: READ
.I /devices/queries/devices/v1
.TP
.B Assets: READ
.I /discover/queries/applications/v1
(Falcon Discover). A 403 here when the scope is ticked means Discover is not
licensed.
.TP
.B IOC Management: READ
.I /iocs/queries/indicators/devices/v1
for the reserved domain
.BR example.com .
The service's own 404 (its JSON answer, with a trace ID) is the expected
"no hosts" answer and counts as OK. A 404 for the route itself, or one from
anything in front of the service, is an ERROR.
.TP
.B Alerts: READ
.I /alerts/queries/alerts/v2
.PP
For each it prints OK, DENIED or ERROR, with a count at most. It then revokes
its token. It never prints the token, the secret, an ID or a record.
.PP
.B \-\-find\-app
answers "do we run this?" from Falcon Discover: every installed application
whose name contains
.I NAME
(or equals it, with
.BR \-\-exact ),
with its host count, top versions and platforms. Over
.B \-\-max\-rows
it says the counts are a lower bound.
.PP
.B \-\-new\-apps
answers "what appeared that we never had?": applications first seen in the
last
.I DAYS
(1 to 90) with no record from before the window. It also lists the ones it
could not check (no vendor, a name a lookup refuses, or over the cap), which
should be treated as possibly new, and counts the rest (updates, or new hosts for something already run). It makes at most 200
of those lookups.
.PP
Neither prints a host name or ID. A name or vendor may hold only letters,
digits, space and
.BR ". _ - ( ) / &" ,
2 to 80 characters; anything else is refused before a request, so a name
cannot change the query.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash.
Exactly one of
.BR \-\-check ,
.B \-\-find\-app
or
.B \-\-new\-apps
is required.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check the API client.
.TP
.BI \-\-find\-app " NAME"
List installed applications matching
.IR NAME .
.TP
.BI \-\-vendor " VENDOR"
With
.BR \-\-find\-app :
the vendor must match too.
.TP
.B \-\-exact
With
.BR \-\-find\-app :
name and vendor must equal the values, not contain them.
.TP
.BI \-\-new\-apps " DAYS"
List applications new to the estate in the last
.I DAYS
days.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-rows " N"
Stop reading after
.I N
records. Default: 2000 for
.BR \-\-find\-app ,
10000 for
.BR \-\-new\-apps .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON instead of text.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Give up after this long. Default: 2m, and at least 15m for
.BR \-\-new\-apps .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the environment, or from
.I fleet.env
.RB ( FLEET_ENV ,
or
.I fleet.env
under
.BR FLEET_HOME ).
There is no flag for the secret.
.TP
.B FALCON_BASE_URL
The cloud's API host:
.BR api.crowdstrike.com ,
.BR api.us\-2.crowdstrike.com ,
.B api.eu\-1.crowdstrike.com
or
.BR api.laggar.gcw.crowdstrike.com .
Any other host, a port, a path or credentials in the URL is refused before
a request is made. Redirects are never followed.
.TP
.B FALCON_CLIENT_ID
.TQ
.B FALCON_CLIENT_SECRET
The API client, created with Read scopes only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.BR \-\-check :
the token and all four scopes work.
.BR \-\-find\-app ,
.BR \-\-new\-apps :
the lookup finished, whether or not anything matched.
.TP
.B 1
A setting is missing or refused, the token failed, a scope is denied or
failed, a name was refused, or a lookup failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage: no mode, two modes, or a
.B \-\-find\-app
option without
.BR \-\-find\-app .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the client on the box:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-check
.RE
.PP
The same, as JSON, for a script:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-check \-\-json
.RE
.PP
Do we run Chrome, and which versions?
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-find\-app chrome
.RE
.PP
What appeared this week that we never had before?
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-new\-apps 7
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-agent (1),
RUNBOOK.md section 11j, SECURITY.md.
